The repo implements this as a pause/resume contract around `request_info`.

- Local functional workflows: the workflow calls `ctx.request_info(...)` with a `response_type` and `request_id`, then later resumes with `run(responses={request_id: value})`. In the sample, it asks for `str` feedback and resumes with `responses={"review_request": ...}`; the test shows the first run pausing with `IDLE_WITH_PENDING_REQUESTS` and the resumed run producing the final output ([`python/samples/03-workflows/functional/hitl_review.py:49`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/03-workflows/functional/hitl_review.py:51`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/03-workflows/functional/hitl_review.py:52`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/03-workflows/functional/hitl_review.py:77`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/core/tests/workflow/test_functional_workflow.py:251`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/core/tests/workflow/test_functional_workflow.py:254`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/core/tests/workflow/test_functional_workflow.py:256`](${LOCAL_PATH}

- Hosted Azure Functions: the HITL sample defines typed `HumanApprovalRequest` and `HumanApprovalResponse`, calls `ctx.request_info(..., response_type=HumanApprovalResponse)`, and handles the reply in a typed `@response_handler` ([`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:85`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:100`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:239`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:241`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:247`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:248`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/samples/04-hosting/azure_functions/12_workflow_hitl/function_app.py:253`](${LOCAL_PATH} `AgentFunctionApp` exposes `GET /api/workflow/status/{instanceId}` and `POST /api/workflow/respond/{instanceId}/{requestId}`; status returns `pendingHumanInputRequests`, the POST raises the Durable external event named by `requestId`, and the orchestrator stores pending requests, waits on that event, and reconstructs the JSON into the declared response type ([`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_app.py:454`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_app.py:499`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_app.py:507`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_app.py:532`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_workflow.py:707`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_workflow.py:727`](${LOCAL_PATH} [`python/packages/azurefunctions/agent_framework_azurefunctions/_workflow.py:984`](${LOCAL_PATH}

`WorkflowContext.request_info()` is the core pause/resume hook: it emits a `request_info` event with the request payload and expected response type, and the executor is expected to define a matching `@response_handler` [python/packages/core/agent_framework/_workflows/_workflow_context.py:367](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/packages/core/agent_framework/_workflows/_workflow_context.py:374](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/packages/core/agent_framework/_workflows/_workflow_context.py:392](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/packages/core/agent_framework/_workflows/_workflow_context.py:396](${LOCAL_PATH}

In the non-hosted sample, `TurnManager.on_agent_response()` pauses with `response_type=str`, `on_human_feedback()` receives `feedback: str`, and the driver resumes the workflow with `workflow.run(stream=True, responses=pending_responses)` [python/samples/03-workflows/human-in-the-loop/guessing_game_with_human_input.py:127](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/samples/03-workflows/human-in-the-loop/guessing_game_with_human_input.py:136](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/samples/03-workflows/human-in-the-loop/guessing_game_with_human_input.py:144](${LOCAL_PATH}

